	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>Heri ad me tuę literę<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1">Nicht erhalten.</note> perlatae sunt, humanissime pater.</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Nuncium, quem misisti, ad <persName ref="p1057">Vulpium</persName>, <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>quamprimum domum rediit, perduxi<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2">Der Überbringer von <persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> nicht erhaltener Antwort auf <persName ref="p1057">Peter Fuchs</persName>' Brief vom 15. Oktober (oben <ref target="file11847">Nr. 1801</ref>) ist nicht bekannt.</note>.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Valemus recte omnes; in statu felici res meę po<lb xml:id="p1z3"/>sitae sunt ut semper, gratia deo.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Chara vero sunt apud nos omnia.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">De rebus, quae ubique hodie <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>novę feruntur, hi sunt apud nos rumores: Chares nostros numatos<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3">Mit den begüterten Kariern sind die Profiteure des Solddienstes gemeint; vgl. <bibl source="b8">HBBW VI</bibl> <ref target="file10931">[Nr. 889]</ref>, S. 417, Anm. 7.</note> securos ociososque vitam <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>Epicuream agere, <persName ref="p18538">caesarem</persName><note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4"><persName ref="p18538">Karl V.</persName></note> nobis inimicissimum, ad hunc <placeName ref="l361">Norinbergenses</placeName> una <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>cum <persName ref="p9708">duce</persName> <persName ref="p9708">Wirtenbergensi</persName><note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Herzog <persName ref="p9708">Ulrich von Württemberg</persName>.</note> descivisse; sic indies nostrę religionis homines ad casum inclinari <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>propter <persName ref="p18538">Carlum</persName>.</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la">Quae sive vera sint sive ficta, magna tentatio est; his <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>enim cuniculis<note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6">Vgl. Adagia, 4, 7, 61 (<bibl source="b370">LB</bibl> II 1112).</note> mentes nostrorum <persName ref="p20225">regi</persName><note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7">König <persName ref="p20225">Franz I.</persName> von <placeName ref="l832">Frankreich</placeName>.</note> expugnatas tradere nonnulli nituntur.</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l41">Bernenses</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z9"/>cum <placeName ref="l167">Genevensibus</placeName> iterum dissident;<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8">Vgl. oben <ref target="file11845">Nr. 1799</ref>.</note> quidam illis excidium minantur idque propter novas <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>subinde iniurias.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la">Scripsit mihi nuper d. <persName ref="p8011">Gvaltherus</persName><note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9">Der Brief <persName ref="p8011">Rudolf Gwalthers</persName> an <persName ref="p8082">Frey</persName> ist nicht erhalten.</note> de d. <persName ref="p1974">Luthero</persName>: „Fefelisset me, si amice <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>scripsisset monachus,<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10"><persName ref="p8082">Frey</persName> reagiert auf die Nachricht vom unfreundlichen Schreiben <persName ref="p1974">Luthers</persName> an <persName ref="p4851">Christoph Froschauer</persName> vom 31. August (<bibl source="b671">WA</bibl> Briefwechsel X 384-388, Nr. 3908; vgl. oben <ref target="file11843">Nr. 1797</ref>, 62-104).</note> nam ab illis aliquando extorsi, qui virum maxime cum suis defendunt erroribus, uti <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>faterentur ne quidem dignari illum <placeName ref="l587">Tigurinos</placeName> vel libros vel literas perlegere, sed statim cognitis titulis, quicquid <lb xml:id="p1z13"/>illud est, in tergum reiicere.“</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Nec tamen desunt, quorum corda ad laudes illius<pb type="edition" next="302"/> exultare videas, <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>si recte hic memini, quod de <persName ref="p4968">Fleuriato<note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11">Der gut lesbar geschriebene Name bleibt trotz Nachforschungen rätselhaft. Eine Verschreibung aus "Henrico" o. ä. scheint kaum wahrscheinlich.</note> Glareano</persName> nostro mihi patruus<note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12">Unbekannt.</note> retulit, nempe quod <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>ille, cum <placeName ref="l21">Badenę</placeName> lavaret, a <placeName ref="l587">Tigurino</placeName> quodam, quid de religionis nostrę doctoribus <persName ref="p1974">Luthero</persName> et <persName ref="p4091">Zvinglio</persName> <lb xml:id="p1z16"/>sentiret, interrogatus respondit, scilicet: „Quid aliud, quam quod magni illi viri suis me libris <lb xml:id="p1z17"/>sentire docuerunt?</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la"><persName ref="p1974">Lutherus</persName> enim <persName ref="p4091">Zvinglium</persName> hęreseos accusat, hic rursus illum apostaseos <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>damnat.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Quę, nisi utrumque mendacii redarguere velim, utique vera fatebor.“</s>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la">Atqui quid <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>dicto magis accommodum ad retinendos in cęcitate sua caecos, praesertim ad id <placeName ref="l587">Tigurino</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>obmutescente?</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la">Paulo post itaque patruus meus subiecit: „Tibi, si nostrę esses<note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>In der Vorlage</hi> esse.</note> religionis, modo <lb xml:id="p1z21"/>filium meum instituendum mitterem.“</s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la">Sed similes ubique labra lactucas habent<note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13"><bibl source="b56">Adagia</bibl>, 1, 10, 71 (<bibl source="b370">LB</bibl> II 386f); <bibl source="b473">Otto</bibl> 182f, Nr. 896.</note>.</s>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la">Sequantur, <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>quos admirantur.</s>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="de"><foreign xml:lang="la">Non inveniant, quos fugiunt;</foreign> dann der den kouffman veracht, ist <lb xml:id="p1z23"/>siner whar nit werdt.</s>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la">Ego, quod coepi, nunc magna perago alacritate, cum mundum <lb xml:id="p1z24"/>vanum, deum vero unice verum esse indies addiscam videamque id, quod per Mosen minatus est, <lb xml:id="p1z25"/>verbi sui despectores tanta cęcitate et amentia percuti<note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" n="14">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Dtn 28, 28</ref></cit>.</note>.</s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la">Det tamen ille, qui omnia dedit, <lb xml:id="p1z26"/>mentem omnibus meliorem.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la" ana="salute">Resalutat mea<note xml:id="fn15" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="15"><persName ref="p8082">Freys</persName> Ehefrau ist nicht namentlich bekannt.</note> obsequentissime.</s>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la" ana="salute">Salutant et fratres, domini mei obser<lb xml:id="p1z27"/>vandissimi.</s>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la" ana="salute">Salutabis et tu meo nomine tuos et meos, quibus propter nuncii<note xml:id="fn16" type="footnote" n="16">Unbekannt (vgl. oben Z. 1f).</note> celerem abitum <lb xml:id="p1z28"/>scribere non licuit.</s>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell">Vale.</s>
					<s n="23" xml:lang="la">11. calendas novembreis 1543.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="24" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z29"/>Tuus ex animo <persName ref="p8082">Io. Leop. Fry</persName><note xml:id="fnc" type="footnote" n="c"><hi>Neben der Unterschrift von späterer Hand</hi> <placeName ref="l49">Biellis</placeName>.</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="25" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>Eruditione ac probitate clarissimo <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>d. d. <persName ref="p495">Heinrycho Bullingero</persName>, <placeName ref="l587">Tigurinę</placeName> <lb xml:id="p2z3"/>ecclesię antistiti fidelissimo, domino <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>patrique summe observando.</s>
					<s n="26" xml:lang="de"><lb xml:id="p2z5"/><placeName ref="l587">Zürich</placeName>.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
